{
 "id": 68812,
 "name": "Linked Data Models for Emotion and Sentiment Analysis Community Group",
 "is_closed": true,
 "creation-date": "2014-01-07",
 "description": "<p>The Sentiment Analysis Community Group is a forum to promote sentiment analysis research. Topics addressed are:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Definition of a Linked Data based vocabulary for emotion and sentiment analysis.</li>\r\n\r\n<li>Requirements beyond text-based analysis, i.e. emotion/sentiment analysis from images, video, social network analysis, etc.</li>\r\n\r\n<li>Clarifying requirements and the need for consensus as e.g. systems currently use widely varying features for describing polarity values (1-5, -2/-1/0/1/2, positive/neutral/negative, good/very good etc.).</li>\r\n\r\n<li>Marl and Onyx are vocabularies for emotion and sentiment analysis that can be taken as a starting point for discussion in the CG.</li>\r\n\r\n\r\n     </ul>",
